# rule.require.clamp-edge-cases

## .what
every defect fix clamps its edge case: a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after, committed with the fix
- treat the defect as an edge-case class (boundary, stale ref, empty input, race), not a point event
- the repro that proves the fix IS the clamp — keep it
- prove the clamp bites

## .prove it bites
1. fix lands, clamp green
2. revert only the fix, rebuild, run → MUST go red
3. restore, rebuild, run → MUST go green
step 2 stays green → the clamp does not exercise the defect; rewrite it

## .grain
un-observable in a unit (race, drift, flake)? clamp at the grain that observes it (integration, hermetic temp repo)

## .example
stale-ref scope defect (diff vs local `main`, which lags): fix = compare `origin/main`; clamp = temp repo with local `main` one commit behind; assert only this branch's change matches. revert → red, restore → green

## .enforcement
- defect fix with no regression clamp = blocker (rule.require.test-covered-repairs)
- clamp that passes under the un-fixed defect = blocker
- boundary defect clamped at one value, not the class = nitpick
